WEBVTT

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:03.650
I'm gonna be the first-star idol one day!

00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:07.820
Nijino Yume's about to start her Aikatsu!

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:13.700
Fun! Fun! Cranking Your Heart Full-Throttle!{or "cranking your heart full-throttle"}

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:18.200
Shining with a sensitive vibrato, Yuuki Subaru!

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:23.460
Your little brother straddling the line between cute and cunning, Kasumi Asahi!

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:28.960
The prim and proper prince whose blood runs hot, Igarashi Nozomu!

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:33.970
Engraver of cleverly struck cool dance moves, Kira Kanata.

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:39.220
Welcome back to M4's show, Fun! Fun! Cranking Your Heart Full-Throttle! {that wasn't even consistent}

00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:42.980
What'll today's First Step be?

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:45.730
We'll kick it off with our talk segment!

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:47.900
I still can't believe it.

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:51.990
That hurt, Yume-chan!

00:00:51.990 --> 00:00:54.320
See? You aren't dreaming.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:55.320
Yeah...

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:58.120
We got the offer because of our hard work.

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:00.240
Have a little more confidence in yourself.

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:02.200
I wish I could,

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:06.500
but going on such a popular show makes me feel like I'm going to wake up any second now.

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:11.500
We're going either way, so just make sure they're begging for us idols to come back.

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:14.470
That's right! Let's do our best!

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:15.260
Yeah.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:21.510
Subaru-kyun! The day has finally come!{huh}

00:02:58.280 --> 00:02:59.780
The scripts are here!

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:03.280
Let's see where our parts are.

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:07.750
Looks like we're in the talk, cooking, and singing segments.

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:14.250
Just like with S4, seeing M4 have their own show makes it feel like that's what makes an idol. {this line actually confuses me 王道}{eto confirmed}

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:15.040
Yeah.

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:21.300
Hey, if we ever got a regular show for ourselves, what kind of segments would you want? {and I forget this english term too}{I don't think there is a real one}

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:30.310
Personally, I'd want a traveling segment where I'd get to eat yummy snacks from around the world.{I slightly prefer snacks over sweets for the general translation of okashi}

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:36.110
And then another segment about going out to discover yummy snacks around the world...

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:38.230
Sure, sure!

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:39.820
It's all about the sweets.

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:43.070
Whoops...

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:44.410
Want some candy?

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:45.450
Thanks.

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:49.700
Come to think of it, isn't that other girl going to be with us too?

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:53.460
The hope of Theater Class who we acted in that drama with.{did we really use "hope of Theater Class" before? there must a better way doesn't it?}

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:56.090
Oh yeah, Ako-chan.

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:58.090
I've made it!

00:03:58.090 --> 00:04:01.920
I get to be with my dear Subaru-kyun meow!

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:07.600
Everything about Subaru-kyun is recorded in the database of my heart.

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:10.100
Subaru-kyun's favorite food is...

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:14.100
"Bananas to give me the power to sing at my performances."

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:16.860
Yes, of course! I know very well.

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:20.860
Your favorite color is that of the cloudless heavens, sky blue! {or, I mean, clear skies}

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:23.280
You're a huge fan of action movies!

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:27.240
But every once in a while, you like to get your horror fix.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:30.120
And all you read is sci-fi! {or SciFi, or SyFy...}{why would any from of those be optiones}

00:04:32.210 --> 00:04:34.080
Now to capture the limelight—

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:38.630
No, I will capture Subaru-kyun's heart all for myself!

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:41.170
I can't wait meow!{that wasn't even a real pun}

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:46.260
Come to think of it, Nijino Yume will be there too.{what is with you and unidiomatic usages of words from a slightly formal register}

00:04:46.470 --> 00:04:48.220
You can have this.

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:51.310
That was dangerous!

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:55.190
I absolutely refuse to lose to her.

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:03.530
Now then, time to put my heart into picking the perfect outfit.

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:13.620
The wait is over!

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:16.920
Good morning!

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:21.210
It's been too long! Ako-chan, let's have another—

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:23.130
What?

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:28.890
Nijino Yume! I will not lose to you!

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:31.390
Yes?

00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:34.270
Sup. It's been a while, jumbo ribbon.

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:36.020
Yamaguchi-san!

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:37.980
I'll be counting on you all today.

00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:40.020
Thank you for having us.

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:41.770
Yo!

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:43.820
It's M4!

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:45.530
All of them at once!

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:51.280
Boiled octopus, you'll be in the cooking segment today,
so be careful not to end up as part of the recipe.

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:55.160
Geez, will you give that name a rest al—

00:05:55.160 --> 00:06:00.420
M-My name is Saotome Ako! I'll be giving my utmost to today's production!

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:03.420
It's an honor to be here!

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:06.300
You're really into this. Nice to meet you.

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:08.430
Ako, right?

00:06:09.010 --> 00:06:09.930
Yes!

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:12.560
Talk about a complete one-eighty.

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:13.930
For sure.

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:19.190
Well, this is just a variety show, 
so don't worry and have fun with it.

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:21.110
We'll see you in a bit.

00:06:21.110 --> 00:06:23.360
Don't mess up, boiled octo.{should actually we in capitalize this?}

00:06:26.440 --> 00:06:28.450
Let's meet up in five.

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:29.200
Okay!

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:35.080
Nice! I got Subaru-kyun to remember my name!

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:38.540
Ako! Ako! Ako-meow!

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:44.920
Wh-What are you looking at?

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:47.590
I just noticed you were cute as usual.

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:03.610
For the most part, we'll just follow the script.

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:06.980
Unless <i>somebody</i> knocks us off the rails.

00:07:06.980 --> 00:07:08.820
Like Subaru-kun over here.

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:10.360
I never do that!

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:12.320
<i>Subaru-kyun!</i>

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:15.870
<i>That's right, this is why I enrolled in this school—</i>

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:18.870
<i>Subaru-kyun,</i>

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:21.250
<i>it was all so I could meet you.</i>

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:27.380
<i>And now my dear Subaru-kyun is within arm's reach!</i>

00:07:27.710 --> 00:07:30.380
<i>My, I'm so happy!</i>

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:31.550
Excuse me.

00:07:32.090 --> 00:07:33.390
What is it?

00:07:33.390 --> 00:07:36.640
What do these blank lines mean?

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:39.390
Oh, that's free talk.

00:07:39.390 --> 00:07:41.890
You can say whatever you want there.

00:07:41.890 --> 00:07:47.070
And sometimes the floor director holds up cue cards like this.

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:48.900
Be on the lookout for it.

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:54.910
And I'm sure you already know, but the light on the cameras means that it's rolling.

00:07:54.910 --> 00:07:56.280
I didn't, actually.

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:58.160
Okay, I understand.

00:07:58.160 --> 00:08:01.160
But honestly, you don't need to stress yourselves out.

00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:04.920
Be sure to get us some laughs with your usual gags, boiled octopus.

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:09.050
Read my lips: I am not a boiled octopus!

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:11.840
Huh, then what are you? A pickled octopus?

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:13.050
Or maybe fried!

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:14.430
Why more octopuses?!

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:18.180
So cute.

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:31.530
Hello, everyone.

00:08:31.530 --> 00:08:37.070
Welcome to another episode of M4's 
Fun! Fun! Cranking Your Heart Full-Throttle!

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:41.830
We've invited a few rising idols from Four Star Academy's girls division.

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:43.830
We're happy to be here!

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:49.630
Yeah, let's see...

00:08:49.630 --> 00:08:54.340
How about telling everyone what you've been into lately? We'll start with Nijino-san.

00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:56.720
Something I'm into? Well...

00:08:56.720 --> 00:08:59.850
I've been positively hooked on bananas these days!

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:02.680
Huh? You mean like as a food?

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:07.610
Correct! Bananas are the best way to restore your stamina, right Subaru-kun?

00:09:07.610 --> 00:09:13.030
Oh yeah, I do see you eating bananas pretty often, Subaru-kun.

00:09:13.030 --> 00:09:14.990
That's 'cause when I eat bananas—

00:09:14.990 --> 00:09:16.910
They fill you with power, right?

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:18.740
It's the same for me too!

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:20.780
Oh, really now?

00:09:20.780 --> 00:09:23.330
Then maybe I'll try that next time.

00:09:23.910 --> 00:09:27.500
Sakuraba-san, have you read any interesting books lately?

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:29.380
Actually...

00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:31.750
I'm a sci-fi nut myself.

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:34.010
Don't you like the genre as well, Subaru-kun?

00:09:34.010 --> 00:09:35.010
Yeah...

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:38.840
And there's nothing like action films, 
albeit with some horror sprinkled in, right?

00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:39.760
Yeah.

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:43.270
It sounds like you know everything about Subaru-kun.

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:47.520
I happened to come across a magazine that had an interview with him.

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:49.400
I just <i>happened</i> to read it.

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:52.270
Um, so...

00:09:55.650 --> 00:10:02.410
That reminds me, didn't you announce a new song at the Volleyball World Championship's opening ceremony?

00:10:02.410 --> 00:10:07.370
That's right. Our song's about the unity of a team.

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:11.170
Have any of you played volleyball before?

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:15.380
I have! I was in the volleyball club back in elementary school.

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:17.260
Oh, were you?

00:10:17.260 --> 00:10:21.720
I'm proud to say that I never missed a single day of practice.

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:24.680
Not a single one? That is amazing.

00:10:25.060 --> 00:10:31.440
So whenever I start to feel lazy, I motivate myself by thinking back to my days in the club.

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:36.280
That explains where your boundless energy comes from.

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:38.450
Guess you can't judge a book by its cover.

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:40.700
Hey, what's that supposed to mean?

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:43.450
Exactly what it sounds like.

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:44.700
Come on!

00:10:50.710 --> 00:10:55.210
<i>You continue to get in my way, Nijino Yume! {foil my plans, etc}</i>

00:10:55.210 --> 00:10:57.420
We'll break for ten minutes!

00:10:57.420 --> 00:11:02.220
We're jumping straight into the cooking segment after, so please get ready.

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:07.930
Hey.

00:11:08.730 --> 00:11:10.270
What do you want?

00:11:10.270 --> 00:11:14.480
You're a die-die-diehard fan of Subaru, aren't you?{...i'll accept it}

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:16.230
Wh-What?

00:11:16.230 --> 00:11:17.860
You're so transparent.

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:20.530
But keep it under control.

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:22.240
When we're on that side of the cameras,

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:25.240
all of us are equal as idols.

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:29.620
I can't say I understand what you're trying to imply.

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:50.640
It's time for the cooking battle you've all been waiting for!

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:57.020
So, usually we'd have M4 split up into two teams and compete,

00:11:57.020 --> 00:12:00.900
but today we'll be having our guests cook.

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:03.280
And that leaves us to judge!

00:12:03.280 --> 00:12:07.160
We're all excited to see what the girls whip up for us.

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:11.460
Let's have them draw lots for their teams. Go ahead.

00:12:18.130 --> 00:12:20.420
Now let's get this going!

00:12:20.420 --> 00:12:22.840
Cooking, start!

00:12:24.010 --> 00:12:25.550
What should we make?

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:28.510
Let's see, please give me a moment.

00:12:28.510 --> 00:12:31.430
I need to run a full scan of my brain data.

00:12:31.430 --> 00:12:33.560
Subaru-kyun's favorite food...

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:36.690
Tick tick tick tick...

00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:36.690
Huh? Hey, are you okay?

00:12:39.270 --> 00:12:40.190
Ding-ding!

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:44.570
Let's make Subaru-kyun's favorite foods, egg dishes!

00:12:44.570 --> 00:12:47.830
Sure, sounds good! What exactly should we do?

00:12:47.830 --> 00:12:50.160
Leave the omelettes to me.

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:52.410
Please take care of the tamagoyaki. {let it be known that etoce did this}

00:12:52.410 --> 00:12:54.670
We're both making eggs dishes?

00:12:54.670 --> 00:12:56.580
Yes, but of course.

00:12:56.580 --> 00:12:58.210
Okay, got it!

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:05.720
<i>Subaru-kyun! Ako's fluffy omelettes will be ready for you in no time!</i>

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:09.850
What's wrong, Subaru-kun?

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:12.220
I just got the chills.

00:13:12.220 --> 00:13:14.980
Because you're getting the chance to eat Yume-chan's cooking?

00:13:14.980 --> 00:13:16.350
Don't be stupid.

00:13:21.110 --> 00:13:24.490
<i>I can only hope she's thought this through.</i>

00:13:26.820 --> 00:13:31.450
<i>Eggs, eggs, in the pan! Be the fluffiest in all the land!{eier, eier in dem pfann', sei die flaumigst' im ganzen land}</i>

00:13:33.290 --> 00:13:34.710
Is something the matter?

00:13:34.710 --> 00:13:38.380
I had the heat on too high and burned the eggs.

00:13:41.250 --> 00:13:42.710
What now?

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:46.880
Allow me to run another full scan of my brain database.

00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:48.010
O-Okay.

00:13:48.010 --> 00:13:50.470
Tick tick tick tick...

00:13:50.470 --> 00:13:51.510
Ding-ding!

00:13:51.510 --> 00:13:52.770
Leave it to me!

00:13:55.520 --> 00:13:59.650
We'll turn this into scrambled eggs and use them for egg sandwiches instead.

00:13:59.650 --> 00:14:00.440
Sure!

00:14:01.650 --> 00:14:02.900
Done!

00:14:02.900 --> 00:14:04.780
And done!

00:14:09.780 --> 00:14:12.080
On to taste testing!

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:15.540
Hand-rolled sushi! So we can pick what we want ourselves.

00:14:16.040 --> 00:14:21.000
How naïve of them to make sushi for Subaru-kyun of all people.

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:23.210
We've got this one clinched.

00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:24.550
Let's hope so.

00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:31.050
Hey, Subaru-kun. You stuffed too much into that one.

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:38.560
This taste reminds me of field trips in elementary school.

00:14:38.560 --> 00:14:40.060
What kind of taste is that?

00:14:40.060 --> 00:14:41.690
It's really good!

00:14:43.400 --> 00:14:47.570
But wait, weren't you going to make something else at first?

00:14:50.820 --> 00:14:52.570
Time for the results!

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:56.580
And there you have it, a tie!

00:15:00.460 --> 00:15:02.580
Isn't that great? We tied.

00:15:05.630 --> 00:15:07.970
No, we lost.

00:15:15.600 --> 00:15:18.430
Eggs and more eggs? Give me a break.

00:15:18.430 --> 00:15:21.400
That was all intended for Subaru.

00:15:22.270 --> 00:15:25.520
You really can't see anything but him.

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:27.610
Is that a problem?

00:15:27.990 --> 00:15:32.610
Tell me something. Why did you become an idol? {damn}

00:15:35.740 --> 00:15:38.370
You doing it for Subaru or something?

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:40.370
Is that enough for you?

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:43.960
All we have left is the singing segment.

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:57.640
I'm sorry for messing up like that! I'm the reason we couldn't win.

00:15:57.640 --> 00:16:01.020
You have nothing to apologize for.

00:16:01.020 --> 00:16:02.060
Huh?

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:05.560
I may have been too fixated on eggs.

00:16:06.060 --> 00:16:09.650
Next is the singing segment. Let's try to put this behind us and move on.

00:16:09.650 --> 00:16:11.740
Yeah, you're right.

00:16:12.820 --> 00:16:17.160
But I'm so nervous it feels like my heart's going to jump out of my throat!

00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:22.710
At times like that, you should take a deep breath

00:16:22.710 --> 00:16:26.670
and imagine yourself singing like you would on any other day.

00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:28.630
Okay, I'll give it a shot.

00:16:34.180 --> 00:16:35.140
It worked!

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:36.050
See?

00:16:36.050 --> 00:16:43.140
This just makes me respect how well you can act in front of such huge audiences, Ako-chan.

00:16:43.690 --> 00:16:45.440
Do you mind if I call you that?

00:16:45.440 --> 00:16:47.940
I don't mind, Koharu.

00:16:49.780 --> 00:16:53.030
Ako-chan, I'm going to get some fresh air.

00:16:53.030 --> 00:16:55.030
Are you still nervous?

00:16:55.030 --> 00:16:57.280
No, I'm fine now.

00:17:03.580 --> 00:17:04.750
A script. {it's actually yume's so she can't rightfully say "her", even if it's wrong}

00:17:08.290 --> 00:17:11.300
I only looked at Subaru-kyun's lines.

00:17:24.770 --> 00:17:28.770
She really worked to prepare for this.

00:17:32.440 --> 00:17:35.150
<i>Compared to her, I...</i>

00:17:41.910 --> 00:17:44.910
<i>What have I been doing?</i>

00:17:49.580 --> 00:17:52.250
Did you see it? This is so embarrassing!

00:17:52.250 --> 00:17:57.050
You saw all my weird scribbles and pronunciation guides, didn't you?

00:17:57.050 --> 00:17:59.470
Yes, I was rather surprised.

00:17:59.470 --> 00:18:01.050
Aw man...

00:18:02.180 --> 00:18:07.480
<i>What surprised me wasn't your notes, but the amount of effort you put in.</i>

00:18:09.480 --> 00:18:12.150
It's time for the singing segment.

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:13.940
Yeah, let's do our best!

00:18:13.940 --> 00:18:18.110
<i>Yes, I will sing for myself today.</i>

00:18:18.110 --> 00:18:20.950
<i>I will stand on that stage as an idol.</i>

00:18:26.460 --> 00:18:27.960
I'm going to get ready.

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:33.550
Does she seem a bit different to you?

00:18:33.550 --> 00:18:34.300
Yeah.

00:18:34.300 --> 00:18:37.380
All right, I'm gonna buckle down too!

00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:45.270
Saotome Ako, making her dazzling entrance!{or if you don't must the comma structure, "Saotome Ako makes her dazzling entrance"}

00:21:38.650 --> 00:21:41.400
Wow, so that's what she's like serious.

00:21:42.480 --> 00:21:44.400
She flipped her switch on.

00:21:51.450 --> 00:21:55.460
Good work. Your song was pretty good.

00:22:00.040 --> 00:22:02.210
Ako-chan! That was a great show!

00:22:02.920 --> 00:22:05.130
What are you acting all friendly for?

00:22:05.130 --> 00:22:07.340
Our war is far from over!

00:22:08.840 --> 00:22:10.850
Subaru-kyun!

00:22:11.970 --> 00:22:12.720
I'm sorr—

00:22:15.180 --> 00:22:17.600
You've finally started to act like an idol.

00:22:17.600 --> 00:22:19.980
I don't want to hear that from you.

00:23:58.830 --> 00:24:01.410
Today's most memorable performance

00:24:01.410 --> 00:24:04.670
will get a special call-out by M4's Yuuki Subaru.

00:24:04.670 --> 00:24:09.010
Your stage that practically screamed 
"It's summer!" from the beach was awesome!

00:24:10.840 --> 00:24:14.140
I got the chance to help out with the admins' work! {managers? leaders?}

00:24:14.140 --> 00:24:16.810
Yume-chan's Dress Make Seminar!

00:24:16.810 --> 00:24:17.850
Just kidding!

00:24:18.770 --> 00:24:20.770
Next time on Aikatsu Stars!

00:24:20.770 --> 00:24:22.390
Together with Yuri-chan.

00:24:22.390 --> 00:24:24.440
Become the first-star idol!
